Hello Frederik,

On Fri, 16 Sep 2016 15:18:21 +0200, Frederik Aalund wrote:
> The PYTHON3_PYC_ONLY option did the following:
>     * Compile `*.py` into `__pycache__/*.pyc` files
>     * Delete `*.py` files
> 
> I've changed it to do the following:
>     * Compile `*.py` into `*.pyc` files
>     * Delete `*.py` files
> 
> The problem with the old behaviour is that python does *not* look
> into the `__pycache__` directory if the `*.py` file is missing.
> Python will, however, find a `*.pyc` file where the `*.py` file was
> supposed to be. This is by design (PEP 3147).
> 
> The change of behaviour in this patch is accomplished by passing
> `legacy=True` to `compileall`. I've adopted `compileall`'s command
> line interface for `pycompile` and used `-b` to denote `legacy=True`.
> 
> Signed-off-by: Frederik Aalund <fpa@sbtaqua.com>

